    "description": "Kenya's current national curriculum, phased in from 2017, replacing 8-4-4. Structure: 2 years Pre-Primary (PP1-PP2), 6 years Primary (Grade 1-6, split Lower Primary 1-3 / Upper Primary 4-6), 3 years Junior Secondary (Grade 7-9), 3 years Senior Secondary (Grade 10-12) with three pathways (STEM, Social Sciences, Arts and Sports Science). Junior Secondary was rationalised in 2024 from 14 optional learning areas to 9 compulsory ones — this seed reflects the current, post-2024 structure. As of this seed date, the first CBC cohort reached Grade 10 in January 2026; Grade 11 and Grade 12 have no enrolled cohort yet (expected January 2027 and January 2028 respectively) and are marked inactive with no subjects populated, since their exact rollout subject lists are not yet independently confirmable — see the verification doc's gaps section.",
